# qwen3.5:9b-64k — Qwen3.5 9B with a 64K context window baked in.
# This is the DEFAULT offline brain (2026-06-15). Qwen3.5 9B was never the
# problem — the 256K variant was: at 256K the q8_0 KV cache is ~16GB, so the
# model loaded ~22GB on the 36GB M5 Max, pinned GPU/RAM, thrashed, and every
# request crawled. 64K holds the full-harness prompt (~30-50K) with headroom
# while keeping KV ~5GB → ~12GB loaded total → comfortable and responsive.
# Native context is 256K, so 64K incurs NO rope-scaling penalty.
# Baked here (not via OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH) so the global 32768 default stays
# correct for the qwen2.5 coders.
# Build: modelfiles/build.sh qwen3.5-9b-64k.Modelfile
#
# THIS TAG IS BUILT WITHOUT THE SHARED SYSTEM PROMPT as of 2026-08-16. It is in
# build.sh's BARE_TAGS list, so the script skips the SYSTEM append for it and a
# plain `ollama create` gives the same result.
#
# Why: the prompt only applies when a request sends no system message of its
# own, and both consumers of this tag (`/model qwen-9b` and the fusion-qwen
# subagent) always send one. That left bare `ollama run` as the only thing it
# could serve, and on a 9B that meant 43,092 tokens of prefill — 8+ minutes,
# ending in a 500. Stripped, the same call is 12 tokens and 2.4 seconds.
#
# It also carried a real hazard: `FROM qwen3.5:9b-64k` would inherit all 43K
# tokens, which is the bug documented in bare/qwen3.8-27b-bare.Modelfile.
#
# The 4B tiers keep their baked prompt — bare usage there actually completes.
FROM qwen3.5:9b
PARAMETER num_ctx 65536
